/*
 * Filigree style "Rose in Bloom": a thorned briar stem along each edge with
 * three leaves to an arm, closed buds and open roses. Six corner pieces,
 * exported from the generator page at design/thorn-corners/ (family
 * `rosesInBloom`; see its README to regenerate) and copied here verbatim as
 * path data: all solid `currentColor` fills, no strokes. A path string that
 * starts with "E:" is drawn with fill-rule="evenodd" (the forward-facing
 * roses have cut lines); every other path is a plain fill.
 *
 * Unlike the single-piece styles, this one exports CORNER_PIECES instead of
 * CornerArt: FiligreeCorners picks one piece per corner and may mirror it
 * across the diagonal (see ../Filigree.jsx). It has no divider of its own:
 * ./index.js gives it Thorned Bramble's. Plain data with no JSX, so Node
 * scripts (scripts/design-check.mjs) can import CORNER_SIZE from it.
 */

/*
 * Corners are drawn 134px (CORNER_SIZE), larger than the other styles'
 * 112px; the size belongs to this style, so the divider and Art Deco keep
 * theirs.
 */
export const CORNER_SIZE = 134;
export const CORNER_VIEWBOX = "0 0 100 100";

/*
 * Frame metrics, as in bramble.jsx: a 2px frame line whose corner is at
 * (20,20) in the 100 box. The arms reach up to about 99 units along each
 * edge, so a framed box should be at least FRAME_MIN_SPAN corner sizes (about
 * 215px) tall and wide, or the arms along one edge run into each other.
 */
export const FRAME_BORDER = "border-2";
export const FRAME_BORDER_WIDTH = 2;
export const FRAME_INSET = 0.2;
export const FRAME_MIN_SPAN = 1.6;

